      "mentions": 17,
      "title": {
        "en": "Attentive clinicians with mixed feedback"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "The majority of clients express deep appreciation for the veterinary team in Lakeview, citing Dr. Angie Duke, Dr. Coulombe, and Dr. Alore for their expertise and kindness. Pet owners report that practitioners listen carefully and provide steady reassurance. However, three critical reviews report negative interactions, alleging unprofessional conduct or medical oversights."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 12,
      "title": {
        "en": "Fear-free techniques and feline rooms"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet parents frequently highlight the gentle handling of reactive dogs and timid cats. Clients appreciate the dedicated feline wing equipped with calming pheromones and videos, as well as Fear Free handling techniques used during examinations. Conversely, two critical reviews describe traumatic patient outcomes following diagnostic procedures and surgery."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "communication",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 8,
      "title": {
        "en": "Responsive updates alongside communication lapses"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners often praise the clinic's prompt laboratory follow-ups and transparent discussions regarding treatment options and diagnostic findings. At the same time, dissatisfied clients report significant communication breakdowns, including a lack of proactive discussion about surgical complications, procedural risks, or post-operative patient status."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Does Duke Animal Hospital accommodate cats in separate exam rooms?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, reviewers highlight a dedicated cat wing featuring calming pheromones and videos designed to reduce feline anxiety."
      },
